{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"{\n\"additions\": [\n{\n\"unit_key\": \"Ch4:1\",\n\"studies\": [\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0517\",\n\"contribution\": \"提供NSCLC队列中抗生素暴露导致PD-L1高表达（≥50%）人群OS显著缩短的实证，揭示宿主生物标志物状态与微生物组干预效应的高度情境依赖性。\"\n},\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0547\",\n\"contribution\": \"通过系统综述量化多数实体瘤中抗生素暴露导致生存率下降的风险幅度，并指出黑色素瘤中的阴性结果，警示单一机制模型的外推边界。\"\n}\n]\n},\n{\n\"unit_key\": \"Ch4:2\",\n\"studies\": [\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0339\",\n\"contribution\": \"整合33项研究Meta分析数据（OS HR=1.31, PFS HR=1.30），量化PPI使用与ICI生存结局的负相关，强调基线或ICI前60天内使用时窗的决定性作用。\"\n},\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0289\",\n\"contribution\": \"描述PPI促进口腔细菌定植、降低α多样性的机制证据，结合P0537构建“胃酸抑制→菌群失调→免疫priming受损”的逻辑链。\"\n},\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0088\",\n\"contribution\": \"提供PPI改变乳酸杆菌科和韦荣球菌属相对丰度的微生物组数据，支持PPI诱导特定菌群失调从而干扰免疫稳态的生物学基础。\"\n}\n]\n},\n{\n\"unit_key\": \"Ch4:3\",\n\"studies\": [\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n\"contribution\": \"报告FMT-LUMINate试验中响应者基线有害菌种丢失及供体菌株未定植的现象，为剖析商业益生菌/补充剂的矛盾证据提供关键对照。\"\n},\n{\n\"source_handle\": \"P0224\",\n\"contribution\": \"简述昼夜节律紊乱与心理压力通过HPA轴激活、LPS易位及SCFAs下降间接调制免疫稳态的潜在路径，指出生活方式干预需纳入多维宿主状态评估框架。\"\n}\n]\n}\n]\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants to select literature cases for a specific chapter unit in a long-form review.\nThe current task is `case_groups` for `Ch4:1`, `Ch4:2`, and `Ch4:3`. Wait, the prompt says \"当前任务：case_groups\" and provides a JSON with `chapter_id: \"Ch4\"` and `unit_catalog` containing 3 units (`Ch4:1`, `Ch4:2`, `Ch4:3`).\nHowever, the instruction says: \"当前调用只负责一个 chapter_id；完整 source_routing 可能已按章节截取，不能据此虚构遗漏来源。\" And the output contract says `bounded_unit_count: 3`. I need to provide additions for these units based on the provided `source_materials`.\n\nLet's look at the units:\nUnit Ch4:1: External factors interfering with microbiome-immune axis (Antibiotics). Substantive point: Antibiotic exposure timing/duration determines negative impact on ICI efficacy, tumor-type specific. Cases already have P0575, P0061, P0275.\nUnit Ch4:2: PPIs. Substantive point: PPIs reduce gastric acid, promote oral bacteria translocation, loss of diversity, independent predictor of decreased ICI efficacy, modulated by prior chemo. Cases already have P0339, P0537, P0286.\nUnit Ch4:3: Diet & Probiotics. Substantive point: High fiber/ketogenic diet enriches SCFA producers or regulates tryptophan metabolism; commercial probiotics show strain-specific/context-dependent effects. Cases already have P0155, P0249, P0390.\n\nI need to pick additional studies from `source_routing` that support these units' substantive points, cases, or paragraph briefs.\nLet's check available sources in `source_routing`:\nP0517: NSCLC, antibiotics, PD-L1 expression. Supports Ch4:1 (antibiotics timing/window, tumor specificity).\nP0522: Review on microbiome impact on chemo/ICI. General background.\nP0523: Gut-targeted strategies RT+ICI. Mentions ILDR, SCFAs. Not directly Ch4 external factors.\nP0524: Oncologist survey. Mentions antibiotics/PPIs/microbiome perception. Background.\nP0537: PPIs, chemo timing, microbiome signatures. Already in Ch4:2.\nP0543: Review leveraging gut microbiota. Covers antibiotics, PPIs, FMT. Good for background/comparison.\nP0545: Polish melanoma, microbiome, diet. Supports Ch4:3 (diet pattern).\nP0547: Systematic review on antibiotics & ICI. Supports Ch4:1.\nP0548: Review on gut microbiota effect on immunity/therapy. Covers antibiotics, mechanisms.\nP0558: ICI administration timing (circadian). Not directly Ch4 external factors.\nP0560: Gut microbiota & tumor immune escape. Mechanisms.\nP0564: Influence of microbiome & antibiotics on ICI efficacy. Supports Ch4:1.\nP0566: Microbiome prediction in lung cancer. Mentions antibiotics/PPIs.\nP0571: Microbiome & circadian rhythms. Background.\nP0575: Antibiotic timing. Already in Ch4:1.\nP0576: Review antibiotic therapy impact. Supports Ch4:1.\nP0585: JCOG2007 trial ancillary biomarker. Chemio-immunotherapy, microbiome. Supports Ch4:3 or general efficacy.\nP0593: Drug synergy via TME remodeling (Allopurinol/Inosine). Not Ch4.\nP0596: ICI myocarditis genes. Not Ch4.\nP0600: irAEs microbiome. Not Ch4.\nP0604: Tenascin-C in myocarditis. Not Ch4.\nP0605: Microbiome & ICI toxicity. Not Ch4.\n\nWait, the prompt says: \"为已经协调好的写作单元挑选可用文献案例。... 对照已有 cases/supporting_studies 的具体贡献，新论文需补充不同结果、条件、方法、发展阶段或有用对照；仅重复相同概括时留在备选池，additions可为空。\"\nI should pick sources that add value to Ch4:1, Ch4:2, Ch4:3.\n\nFor Ch4:1 (Antibiotics):\n- P0517: Adds PD-L1 expression as an effect modifier for antibiotic impact in NSCLC. Shows context-dependency.\n- P0547: Systematic review quantifying risk across multiple solid tumors, highlights melanoma/HCC exceptions, fluoroquinolone trend.\n- P0564: Systematic review summarizing antibiotic timing/spectrum impact, supports dose-response/timing window.\n- P0576: Narrative review synthesizing preclinical/clinical evidence on antibiotic timing (pre vs concurrent), clarifies mechanism links.\n\nFor Ch4:2 (PPIs):\n- P0339 is already there. P0537 is there. P0286 is there.\n- Are there others? P0566 mentions PPIs reducing PFS/OS in lung cancer. Could support Ch4:2 but maybe redundant.\n- Let's stick to what's clearly useful. P0543 covers PPIs negatively impacting ICI. Might be too general. I'll skip adding more for Ch4:2 if not strictly necessary, or add P0543 for broader context if needed. Actually, the prompt says \"只为具体单元补材料\". I will focus on Ch4:1 and Ch4:3 where gaps might exist or comparisons are needed.\n\nFor Ch4:3 (Diet & Probiotics):\n- P0545: Polish melanoma cohort linking high plant/low dairy diet to better response, population-specific microbiome (P. copri, B. uniformis). Supports dietary patterns and population specificity.\n- P0585: JCOG2007 ancillary study showing specific genera (Fusicatenibacter, Butyricicoccus) linked to OS and lower severe AEs in chemo-immunotherapy. Supports diet/metabolite link (SCFA producers) and regimen specificity.\n- P0543: Reviews diet/probiotics/FMT strategies. Good for comparative context on probiotics vs diet.\n\nLet's construct the additions carefully according to the format.\nFormat:\n```json\n{\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"unit_key\": \"Ch4:1\",\n      \"studies\": [\n        {\"source_handle\": \"P0517\", \"contribution\": \"...\"},\n        {\"source_handle\": \"P0547\", \"contribution\": \"...\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_key\": \"Ch4:3\",\n      \"studies\": [\n        {\"source_handle\": \"P0545\", \"contribution\": \"...\"},\n        {\"source_handle\": \"P0585\", \"contribution\": \"...\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nCheck contributions length: ~30-60 Chinese characters. Explain specific writing purpose.\nP0517 contribution: 提供NSCLC队列中PD-L1高表达（≥50%）人群受抗生素负面影响更显著的实证，揭示宿主生物标志物状态与微生物组干预效应的情境依赖性，支撑Ch4:1关于肿瘤类型特异性及疗效异质性的讨论。\nP0547 contribution: 通过系统综述量化多实体瘤中抗生素暴露导致生存率下降的风险幅度，并识别黑色素瘤与HCC的阴性例外及氟喹诺酮类高风险趋势，为Ch4:1界定抗生素干扰的普遍规律与癌种边界提供流行病学基准。\nP0545 contribution: 基于波兰黑色素瘤队列揭示高植物/低乳制品饮食模式与特定菌群（P. copri, B. uniformis）富集的关联，对比其他人群结果，支撑Ch4:3关于膳食成分定向塑造菌群功能及标志物人群特异性的论证。\nP0585 contribution: 依托JCOG2007 III期试验附属研究数据，展示产丁酸菌属（Fusicatenibacter等）丰度与化疗免疫联合治疗OS延长及严重毒性降低的正向关联，为Ch4:3引入宏量营养素代谢输出与方案特异性响应的临床实证。\n\nCheck constraints:\n- \"每篇写 contribution：约30–60字说明这篇材料能帮助本单元解释什么（具体写作用途），可以提出拟议综合；这段文字是具体写作用途，不是论文结果；\"\n- \"保留每个来源真实的研究类型、对象、设置、条件、方法、结果和限制。\"\n- \"不要写成问答清单。\"\n- \"Return JSON only.\"\n\nLet's refine contributions to strictly match the 30-60 char limit and focus on *writing purpose*.\nP0517: 提供NSCLC队列中PD-L1高表达人群受抗生素负面影响更显著的实证，揭示","role":"assistant"}}],"created":1791151394,"id":"chatcmpl-e89b43c9-a658-9ce2-ab74-6cc21f441a4a","model":"qwen3.7-flash","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":2574,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2048,"text_tokens":2574},"prompt_tokens":93825,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"text_tokens":93825},"total_tokens":96399}}